Before any Azure solution enters production, teams should conduct an Operational Readiness Review (ORR) to confirm that all operational requirements have been satisfied.

An ORR typically verifies:

* Monitoring configuration
* Backup implementation
* Disaster recovery readiness
* Security controls
* Documentation completeness
* Incident procedures
* Support ownership
* Capacity planning

# Real-Life Example:
For example, an enterprise application should not go live until monitoring alerts, backup restoration, and operational documentation have all been validated.

# Real-Life Use Case:
A real-life use case is organizations reducing production incidents by identifying operational gaps before deployment.

Operational readiness reviews improve deployment quality and reduce business risk.
